  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes two gate-based quantum PDE solvers combining finite-difference discretization with classical-to-quantum amplitude encoding and either numerical instantiation or column-by-column decomposition. Experiments solving Poisson, heat, Black–Scholes, and Navier–Stokes equations were run on IBM simulators and the ibm_torino device using up to 14 qubits and up to 256M shots, showing lower RMSE and runtime than a VQE baseline but no demonstrated advantage over classical PDE solvers.",
